WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.659 --> 00:00:05.160
Since Lost ended, the former cast members
have taken their careers in a variety of different

00:00:05.160 --> 00:00:05.820
directions.

00:00:05.960 --> 00:00:07.400
But where is Emilie de Ravin?

00:00:07.560 --> 00:00:11.100
Well, here’s what happened to the actress
who played Claire on Lost.

00:00:11.860 --> 00:00:16.620
Just before the final season of Lost wrapped
up, de Ravin starred in her biggest film role

00:00:16.620 --> 00:00:20.160
to date as Robert Pattinson's love interest
in Remember Me.

00:00:20.660 --> 00:00:26.060
De Ravin told The Independent that while there
were no off-screen sparks between them, their

00:00:26.060 --> 00:00:28.840
on-screen chemistry was the result of a lot
of hard work.

00:00:29.160 --> 00:00:33.300
"We spent a lot of time together, talking
about our characters and their relationship,

00:00:33.340 --> 00:00:35.540
because it's so important to be comfortable
together.

00:00:35.900 --> 00:00:40.390
Then, when we were actually shooting, everything
fell into place and felt natural.

00:00:40.390 --> 00:00:44.180
It didn't ever feel like we were reading a
scene or going through the motions."

00:00:44.540 --> 00:00:50.059
However, de Ravin also said that it was difficult
to establish that rapport due to the legions

00:00:50.060 --> 00:00:52.380
of Twilight fans that plagued the shoot.

00:00:52.700 --> 00:00:56.480
"It was difficult for Rob and I to figure
out the logistics of a rehearsal when you've

00:00:56.480 --> 00:00:58.320
got thousands of people watching.

00:00:58.620 --> 00:01:00.760
Even if you're not looking at them, you're
aware of it.

00:01:01.020 --> 00:01:02.380
It can be hard to focus."

00:01:03.320 --> 00:01:07.460
Unfortunately, after Remember Me, de Ravin
appeared in a string of movies that just never

00:01:07.460 --> 00:01:10.580
seemed to appeal to critics or audiences.

00:01:11.060 --> 00:01:16.140
The Chameleon got terrible reviews, Operation:
Endgame only got a limited release in the

00:01:16.140 --> 00:01:20.640
United States, and Love and Other Troubles
was filmed mostly in Finnish.

00:01:21.100 --> 00:01:26.040
De Ravin's most recent role in a feature film
was in the indie movie The Submarine Kid.

00:01:26.360 --> 00:01:31.060
Though her performance was considered a bright
spot, it too fell flat with critics.

00:01:31.300 --> 00:01:36.740
Still, de Ravin told Film Monthly she's happy
doing smaller films instead of chasing big

00:01:36.740 --> 00:01:38.180
time Hollywood stardom.

00:01:38.300 --> 00:01:39.860
"I love the indie circuit.

00:01:40.000 --> 00:01:45.400
I think there's some amazing sort of younger
or undiscovered talent out there as far as

00:01:45.400 --> 00:01:47.480
directors, and just really edgy scripts.

00:01:47.700 --> 00:01:53.060
They're maybe not going to be as widely released
but just really, really interesting subject

00:01:53.060 --> 00:01:54.930
matter which definitely interests me."

00:01:56.520 --> 00:02:00.990
Lost was a cultural phenomenon, so when the
show ended, many assumed the stars would go

00:02:00.990 --> 00:02:02.520
on to even bigger things.

00:02:02.720 --> 00:02:05.540
Yet, instead, many of them initially struggled.

00:02:05.980 --> 00:02:10.740
Matthew Fox's attempts to become a movie star
fizzled, for instance, while Josh Holloway

00:02:10.750 --> 00:02:12.730
had several projects fail.

00:02:12.730 --> 00:02:16.860
It got to the point where some pundits joked
there was a "Lost Curse."

00:02:17.060 --> 00:02:23.140
And de Ravin wasn't immune: her next project,
Americana, was passed over during pilot season.

00:02:23.400 --> 00:02:26.960
Part of the issue may have been that de Ravin
was typecast.

00:02:27.420 --> 00:02:33.040
Prior to playing the pregnant Claire on Lost,
she also played a pregnant girl in the film

00:02:33.050 --> 00:02:37.250
Brick, and went on to play another pregnant
character in the series Roswell.

00:02:37.250 --> 00:02:38.300
She told GQ,

00:02:38.560 --> 00:02:41.480
"I must have some sort of maternal draw to
me.

00:02:41.480 --> 00:02:45.940
I do love children, but I don't really talk
about that in auditions.

00:02:45.940 --> 00:02:46.440
Hi!

00:02:46.500 --> 00:02:47.500
I really love kids!

00:02:47.620 --> 00:02:48.240
Book me!

00:02:48.380 --> 00:02:50.960
But I keep reading scripts that are like that,
too."

00:02:51.860 --> 00:02:56.060
It's only fitting that de Ravin eventually
turned to fairy tales to break the curse.

00:02:56.160 --> 00:03:01.700
In 2012, de Ravin joined the cast of Once
Upon a Time, which was created by Lost writers

00:03:01.700 --> 00:03:04.100
Edward Kitsis and Adam Horowitz.

00:03:04.560 --> 00:03:08.920
She played Belle for seven seasons on the
hit show which is even longer than she played

00:03:08.920 --> 00:03:10.100
Claire on Lost.

00:03:10.220 --> 00:03:14.700
"It's actually quite fabulous how, as I'm
sure you know, they sort of twist around these

00:03:15.240 --> 00:03:16.500
fairy tale characters."

00:03:16.500 --> 00:03:17.920
She told The Hollywood Reporter,

00:03:18.120 --> 00:03:23.020
"It was just a really awesome journey to be
able to give my own spin on such a special,

00:03:23.020 --> 00:03:25.910
iconic character and to work with such amazing
people."

00:03:27.040 --> 00:03:29.140
De Ravin originally hails from Australia...

00:03:29.620 --> 00:03:32.720
I'm the only Australian who loves peanut butter."

00:03:32.800 --> 00:03:35.760
...which led to a lot of homesickness early
in her career.

00:03:36.140 --> 00:03:37.140
She told The Independent,

00:03:37.400 --> 00:03:39.340
"I don't get home as much as I would like
to.

00:03:39.340 --> 00:03:43.440
I miss my family so much, my ideal holiday
is just to hang out with them."

00:03:44.300 --> 00:03:46.920
Now, though, she has her own family in America.

00:03:47.160 --> 00:03:53.520
After divorcing her first husband, actor Josh
Janowicz, in 2014, de Ravin fell in love with

00:03:53.520 --> 00:03:57.260
The Submarine Kid writer and director Eric
Bilitch.

00:03:57.460 --> 00:04:01.970
They got engaged in 2016, the same year de
Ravin gave birth to their daughter Vera.

00:04:01.970 --> 00:04:07.400
And in 2018, de Ravin celebrated two new milestones:
she gave birth to their son, Theodore, and

00:04:07.400 --> 00:04:09.260
she officially became a U.S. citizen.

00:04:09.680 --> 00:04:12.000
You know what they say: home is where the
heart is.

00:04:12.660 --> 00:04:17.640
In 2017, de Ravin told Entertainment Weekly
that she was finally taking some time off

00:04:17.640 --> 00:04:19.260
of work to focus on her new family.

00:04:19.460 --> 00:04:23.070
"There are things in the works right now,
but I've taken the last few months off to

00:04:23.070 --> 00:04:27.840
be a mom, because I've been working since
I had my daughter a year and a half ago, so

00:04:27.840 --> 00:04:30.220
I was just very excited to be able to do that."

00:04:30.460 --> 00:04:35.720
Since then, she's been true to her word, with
her only recent project being the 2019 TV

00:04:35.720 --> 00:04:37.280
movie A Lover Scorned.

00:04:37.460 --> 00:04:41.900
It looks like this phase of her career will
be all about finding a balance between work

00:04:41.900 --> 00:04:46.710
and family, but with two successful shows
and few solid films under her belt, de Ravin

00:04:46.710 --> 00:04:50.300
still has a bright future in Hollywood if
and when she wants it.

